{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc | sed -n '260,380p;459,490p'; rg -n 'carry-over|rehydrat|:failure' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | head -n 55\"","aggregated_output":"   260\t(defn- write-rows\n   261\t  \"Put the rows of every committed program not yet written into the index\n   262\t   store, oldest first (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 5.1, owner decision 1: rows\n   263\t   every round), so `:yin/address` facts name content the store holds.\n   264\t   `:unwritten` holds those programs' row sets.  A put that fails stops\n   265\t   the writing: it and every later row set stay `:unwritten`, and the\n   266\t   round's failure is stage `:materialize`.  Once nothing is unwritten, a\n   267\t   `:materialize` failure is recovered and cleared.  No publication is\n   268\t   made while anything is unwritten, so a HEAD never moves over a missing\n   269\t   row.\"\n   270\t  [ix round]\n   271\t  (loop [ix ix]\n   272\t    (if-let [row-set (first (:unwritten ix))]\n   273\t      (let [failed (try (vm/materialize-tree! (:content-store ix) row-set)\n   274\t                        nil\n   275\t                        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   276\t                          {:round round\n   277\t                           :stage :materialize\n   278\t                           :root (:root row-set)\n   279\t                           :message (ex-message e)}))]\n   280\t        (if failed\n   281\t          (assoc ix :failure failed)\n   282\t          (recur (update ix :unwritten (comp vec rest)))))\n   283\t      (cond-> (dissoc ix :unwritten)\n   284\t        (= :materialize (:stage (:failure ix))) (dissoc :failure)))))\n   285\t\n   286\t\n   287\t(defn- commit\n   288\t  \"Commit one packet as one transaction; its rows join `:unwritten`, which\n   289\t   the round writes before it publishes (`write-rows`).  A packet that\n   290\t   could not be projected or committed is consumed and recorded as the\n   291\t   failure, never counted, and materializes nothing.\"\n   292\t  [ix packet round]\n   293\t  (try\n   294\t    (let [{:keys [tx-data next-e root row-set]}\n   295\t          (packet->tx-data packet\n   296\t                           (:next-e ix)\n   297\t                           {:session-token (:session-token ix), :round round})\n   298\t          answer (transactor/transact! (get-in ix [:publication :transactor])\n   299\t                                       tx-data)]\n   300\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n   301\t        [(-> ix\n   302\t             (assoc :next-e next-e)\n   303\t             (update :transactions inc)\n   304\t             (update :unwritten (fnil conj []) row-set))\n   305\t         true]\n   306\t        [(assoc ix\n   307\t                :failure {:round round\n   308\t                          :root root\n   309\t                          :stage :transact\n   310\t                          :outcome (:dao.stream/outcome answer)})\n   311\t         false]))\n   312\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   313\t      [(assoc ix\n   314\t              :failure {:round round\n   315\t                        :stage :project\n   316\t                        :message (ex-message e)})\n   317\t       false])))\n   318\t\n   319\t\n   320\t(defn- materialize\n   321\t  \"Drain the intake into the store until it blocks.  Answers how many\n   322\t   payloads it materialized and, when the drain met a gap or a defect, what\n   323\t   it met.  The pool is not kept: its intake is dropped with the round.\"\n   324\t  [content-store pool]\n   325\t  (loop [pool pool\n   326\t         n 0]\n   327\t    (let [{:keys [signal], :as r} (jing/observe-step! content-store pool)]\n   328\t      (case signal\n   329\t        :dao.stream/ok (recur (:state r) (inc n))\n   330\t        :dao.stream/blocked [n nil]\n   331\t        [n signal]))))\n   332\t\n   333\t\n   334\t(defn- publish\n   335\t  \"Publish the covered indexes over every committed transaction through\n   336\t   the round's transactor, drain its intake into the store, and read the\n   337\t   manifest back from it.  Only a publication whose manifest the store\n   338\t   answers becomes the reported one, covering `:published` transactions;\n   339\t   in durable mode the HEAD pointer moves — `after-publish` — only after\n   340\t   that read-back, so a HEAD never names a manifest the store cannot\n   341\t   answer, and a HEAD that cannot be written leaves the round reported\n   342\t   unpublished.\"\n   343\t  [ix round]\n   344\t  (try\n   345\t    (let [{:keys [transactor pool]} (:publication ix)\n   346\t          {:keys [manifest-address]} (transactor/publish! transactor\n   347\t                                                          (:publish-opts ix))\n   348\t          [n defect] (materialize (:content-store ix) pool)]\n   349\t      (if defect\n   350\t        (assoc ix :failure {:round round :stage :materialize :outcome defect})\n   351\t        (do (index/read-manifest (:content-store ix) manifest-address)\n   352\t            (when-some [write-head! (:after-publish ix)]\n   353\t              (write-head! manifest-address))\n   354\t            (assoc ix\n   355\t                   :manifest-address manifest-address\n   356\t                   :published (:transactions ix)\n   357\t                   :published-payloads n))))\n   358\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   359\t      (assoc ix\n   360\t             :failure {:round round :stage :publish :message (ex-message e)}))))\n   361\t\n   362\t\n   363\t(defn- consume\n   364\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium, handing each\n   365\t   to `f` with the indexer; a gap marks the indexer lost, after which no\n   366\t   packet reaches `f`.\"\n   367\t  [indexer f]\n   368\t  (loop [ix indexer]\n   369\t    (let [{:keys [status batch] observer' :observer}\n   370\t          (observer/observe-next (:observer ix))\n   371\t          ix (assoc ix :observer observer')]\n   372\t      (case status\n   373\t        :ok (recur (if (:lost? ix) ix (f ix batch)))\n   374\t        :gap (recur (assoc ix :lost? true))\n   375\t        ix))))\n   376\t\n   377\t\n   378\t(defn step\n   379\t  \"The round's index step: observe every packet `program-out` still holds\n   380\t   for this observer, commit each through the round's publication, publish\n   459\t(defn notice\n   460\t  \"What the round from `before` to `after` must tell the user, or nil: a\n   461\t   lost indexer (the round's code was not indexed), or a new failure (the\n   462\t   round's code was not committed or its publication is not readable).\n   463\t   A failure's `:stage` is `:project`, `:transact`, `:materialize` or\n   464\t   `:publish`.\"\n   465\t  [before after]\n   466\t  (let [{:keys [stage outcome message]} (:failure after)]\n   467\t    (cond\n   468\t      (:lost? after)\n   469\t      (str \"Warning: the code index lost a program batch; this round's code\"\n   470\t           \" was not indexed, and indexing is suspended until (reset)\")\n   471\t\n   472\t      (and (= :materialize (:stage (:failure before))) (nil? (:failure after)))\n   473\t      (str \"Note: the code index caught up: rows of earlier rounds are now\"\n   474\t           \" written, and this round is published\")\n   475\t\n   476\t      (not= (:failure before) (:failure after))\n   477\t      (str \"Warning: this round's code is not in the published code index (\"\n   478\t           (name stage) \" failed\"\n   479\t           (when-let [detail (or message (some-> outcome name))]\n   480\t             (str \": \" detail))\n   481\t           \")\"))))\n831:   — and the indexer is rehydrated from it here, before any evaluation\n832:   is admitted (`yin.repl.index/rehydrate`): `q` answers the previous\n891:               :indexer index/rehydrate (:recovery index-store))\n1753:   published manifest (`yin.repl.index/carry-over`), so a rebuild never\n1762:           (update :indexer index/carry-over (:indexer state)))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"## Verdict: SIGN-OFF GRANTED\n\n| Severity | file:line | Issue | Fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| None | — | No remaining sign-off finding | — |\n\nThe four findings are closed. §5.3 now collects requiring and defining programs to a fixed point, and the prompt test evaluates a reader’s `app/g` after the publisher typed `(require 'base)` separately. The missing-program refusal names `base`.\n\nDeclaring `require` as a free primitive is sound: its profile enters the manifest, its `:module/require` effect enters the derived footprint, and `base` remains pinned under `:yin.module/requires`.\n\nThe unwritten row sets are retried before a later program or name transaction can publish. Both paths gate publication on an empty unwritten set, so a later HEAD cannot move over a missing row. The new test checks that HEAD stays put through failures and then moves once, covering all three programs after recovery.\n\nThe **restart limit is acceptable for L4**: an unpublished transaction is process state and is lost on restart; recovery starts from the last published HEAD. That leaves HEAD naming a valid earlier snapshot. The contract now states the limit. Dart’s key-file permission warning and the HEAD-fold performance limit are also documented.\n\nThis was a read-only diff review. I did not rerun the engineer’s reported green JVM, Node, and Dart lanes."}}
